{
  "name": "What to Expect from a Full Interior Paint Package",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about giving your home a fresh look with a full interior paint job? It's more than just slapping on a new color, and understanding the process can really help. A complete package typically kicks off with a detailed on-site walkthrough. This is where you and the painting pros discuss everything from specific walls, ceilings, and trim to doors and closets. You'll get a written quote that spells out the scope of work, which colors go where, and what kind of paint products will be used. Then comes the prep work: protecting your furniture and floors, filling any dents or holes, sanding, and caulking. Depending on your walls, priming might be necessary before the actual painting begins. Finally, there's the painting itself, usually two coats for a rich finish, followed by a meticulous clean-up and a final walkthrough for any touch-ups. Knowing these steps ensures you're on the same page with your contractor and get the beautiful results you're expecting. If you're tackling multiple rooms or your whole home, having a clear plan upfront makes all the difference.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
